::U6F4_01::Appropriate prescription use requires {=right person, medicine, dose, time/route, and purpose ~sharing ~changing dose ~online purchase}

::U6F4_02::Opioids can cause {=respiratory depression ~guaranteed alertness ~immunity ~only faster breathing}

::U6F4_03::Fentanyl is {=a very potent synthetic opioid ~an OTC vitamin ~a stimulant antidote ~a harmless filler}

::U6F4_04::A counterfeit pill {=may copy a legitimate pill while containing unknown substances ~is verified by appearance ~always comes from a pharmacy ~has predictable potency}

::U6F4_05::Mixing depressants {=can compound sedation and breathing suppression ~always balances effects ~eliminates overdose ~is safe at small doses}

::U6F4_06::Unresponsiveness with slow, gurgling breathing requires {=immediate emergency services ~a cold shower ~waiting ~food}

::U6F4_07::Naloxone {=does not replace emergency care and monitoring ~reverses every substance ~works permanently ~verifies a pill}

::U6F4_08::Secure storage and take-back disposal {=reduce unauthorized access and misuse ~increase potency ~replace labels ~allow sharing}

::U6F4_09::Stigma can {=discourage timely help-seeking ~verify a diagnosis ~reverse overdose ~improve breathing}
